---
description: Jurisdiction pack schema, citations, and test requirements
globs: packs/**/*.yaml
alwaysApply: false
---
- Each rule is a YAML file with id, name, applies_to, trigger, severity,
  status_if_true, deadline, evidence_needed, citations, explain_hints.
- Triggers use the small expression language in clinic/packs.py only
  (field tests, sum/any/count, comparisons). No free-form eval.
- Every citation needs a src label and a URL to a primary source.
- Pack metadata (pack.yaml) must include tax_year, effective_from,
  last_reviewed_by, and version. Stale packs warn in the report footer.
- Cross-border overlaps live in packs/cross-border/ and pair existing
  rule ids; they do not recompute thresholds.
